	(text "=== FBV2-S1 MCU CORE (FBV2-S1-002) - GPIO38/47 RELEASED TO THE COMMUNITY PORT, GPIO46 TAKES THE BACKLIGHT ==="
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.0 30.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb020020-b020-4b20-9b20-000000000020")
	)
	(text "GPIO38 = NATIVE_A and GPIO47 = NATIVE_B leave this sheet as the two native community fast-IO signals (D-084). SX1262_DIO1 no longer reaches the MCU: it terminates on the internal PCAL9535A U2 (D-089), which is sheet 08 and is NOT migrated yet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.0 34.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb020021-b021-4b21-9b21-000000000021")
	)
	(text "GPIO43 (U0TXD) is withdrawn from the community port (D-106) and is internal debug only - TP35 carries the ROM boot log, which is the only view of a first board whose USB does not enumerate. GPIO44 (U0RXD) is IR RX, so UART0 is TX-only; ROM download recovery is via the native USB Serial/JTAG on GPIO19/20, not UART0."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.0 38.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb020022-b022-4b22-9b22-000000000022")
	)
	(text "STRAPS. GPIO0: R2 10k pull-up + SW1 direct to GND, no capacitor (Espressif forbids bulk C here). GPIO46: R108 10k pull-down at the pin, and R109 0R FIT isolates the TPS61169 CTRL so the strap survives even if CTRL sources current - GPIO46 MUST be LOW at reset or Joint Download Boot is unreachable. GPIO3: R110 10k pull-down, LOW selects the USB Serial/JTAG source; external JTAG would land on GPIO39-42, which are I2S. GPIO45: R111 10k DNP, VDD_SPI stays 3.3 V; fit it if the internal pull-down is ever in doubt."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.0 42.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb020023-b023-4b23-9b23-000000000023")
	)
)
